 Response:\nInclusion Criteria:\n - Patients\' age from 18 to 60 years old,\n - physical status ASA I-II (by the American Society of Anesthesiologists),\n - Elective unilateral open inguinal hernia repair,\n - Under spinal anesthesia\nExclusion Criteria:\n - age < 18 [OR] or > 60,\n - American society of anesthesiologist (ASA)class III-IV,\n - known allergy to amino amide local anesthetics,\n - skin infection [OR] and diseases at site of injection.\n - coagulation disorders,\n - patients with body mass index (BMI) > 35 kg/m2,\n - scrotal hernias,<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
 - Patients' age from 18 to 60 years old,
 - physical status ASA I-II (by the American Society of Anesthesiologists),
 - Elective unilateral open inguinal hernia repair,
 - Under spinal anesthesia
Exclusion Criteria:
 - age < 18 [OR] or > 60,
 - American society of anesthesiologist (ASA)class III-IV,
 - known allergy to amino amide local anesthetics,
 - skin infection [OR] and diseases at site of injection.
 - coagulation disorders,
 - patients with body mass index (BMI) > 35 kg/m2,
 - scrotal hernias,
